# `dqcoeff` hoisted into the per-thread `TxScratch` — paired A/B.
#
# host  : mac (Apple M4 Pro, aarch64-apple-darwin)
# tool  : tools/perf_ab.sh — interleaved paired rounds, order randomised per
#         round, one untimed warmup inside each sample, NEITHER SIDE NICED,
#         no -C target-cpu=native
# base  : the tile-buffer reservation commit   cand: + this hoist
# grid  : gradient qp 40; still 256/512 x p{2,6,10} n=15,
#         videokey (SVTAV1_VIDEO=1) 128/256/512 x p{6,8} n=25
# ident : Y on all twelve cells
#
# WHY THIS SITE. `tx_unit_inner` is the largest allocation SITE in the whole
# encoder — 72,919 calls to the allocator on ONE 512x512 video-mode key frame
# at preset 8 (heaptrack --print-allocators on r7900x). It allocated three
# `Vec`s per transform unit; `TxScratch`'s doc comment claimed two. `dqcoeff`
# is the miscounted one: written by the quantizer, read by the `dq_full` fold
# and the frequency-domain SSE, returned to nobody.
#
# RESULT
#   still     256 p2 1.014x | 256 p6 1.022x | 256 p10 1.006x
#             512 p2 1.007x | 512 p6 1.009x | 512 p10 1.003x
#   videokey  128 p6 1.007x | 128 p8 1.009x | 256 p6 0.998x
#             256 p8 1.004x | 512 p6 1.003x | 512 p8 1.006x
#
# Four of six STILL cells have their whole p25/p75 span below 1.0; both
# exceptions are p10, where the trellis barely runs. The VIDEOKEY arm is
# NULL-to-marginal — five of six move the right way, every span but 128 p8's
# crosses 1.0.
#
# WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED. That removing the OTHER two allocations at this
# site (`qcoeff`, `recon`) would scale this by 3x. They are moved into the
# returned `TxUnitOut` and escape the `TX_SCRATCH.with` closure, so hoisting
# them needs a different mechanism than this one — and the thread-local Vec
# POOL that mechanism would most obviously be has already measured NULL once
# (benchmarks/alloc_bufpool_null_2026-08-13.meta). Do not assume; measure.
